\q2 take offerings, and go into his courts. 
\q1
\v 9 Worship the Lord in his holy court: 
\q2 let all the earth tremble before him. 
\q1
\v 10 Say among the nations, The Lord reigns: 
\q2 for he has established the world so that it will not be moved: 
\q2 he will judge the people in righteousness. 
\q1
\v 11 Let the heavens rejoice, and the earth exult; 
\q2 let the sea be moved, and its fulness. 
\q1
\v 12 The plains will rejoice, and all things in them: 
\q2 then all the trees of the wood will exult before the presence of the Lord: 
\q1
\v 13 for he comes, for he comes to judge the earth; 
\q2 he will judge the world in righteousness, 
\q2 and the peoples with his truth. 
\c 96 
\d
\v 1 Of David, when his land is established.
