\q1
\v 5 For the Lord is good, 
\q2 his mercy is forever; 
\q2 and his truth to generation and generation. 
\c 100 
\d
\v 1 A Psalm of David. 
\q1
\v 1b I will sing to you, O Lord, of mercy and judgment; 
\q2 I will sing a psalm, 
\q1
\v 2 and I will act wisely in a blameless way. 
\q2 When will you come to me? 
\q2 I walked in the integrity of my heart, in the midst of my house. 
\q1
\v 3 I have not set before my eyes any unlawful thing; 
\q2 I have hated transgressors. 
\q1
\v 4 A perverse heart has not clung to me; 
\q2 when the evil one turned away from me,
\q2 I did not know him.
\q1
\v 5 He who secretly speaks against his neighbour, him I drove away:
\q2 he who is proud-eyed and insatiable in heart,—I did not eat with him.
\q1
\v 6 My eyes are upon the faithful of the land, for them to dwell with me: 
\q2 he who walks in a perfect way,—he ministers to me. 
\q1
\v 7 He who acts proudly didn't dwell in the midst of my house; 
\q2 he who speaks unjust things didn't prosper in my sight. 
\q1
