\q2 that I might destroy out of the city of the Lord all who work lawlessness. 
\c 101 
\d
\v 1 A Prayer for the Poor; when he is deeply afflicted, and pours out his supplication before the Lord. 
\q1
\v 2 Hear my prayer, O Lord,
\q2 and let my cry come to you. 
\q1
\v 3 Don't turn your face away from me: 
\q2 in the day I am afflicted, incline your ear to me: 
\q2 in the day I call on you, speedily hear me. 
\q1
\v 4 For my days have vanished like smoke, 
\q2 and my bones have been parched like a stick. 
\q1
\v 5 I am blighted like grass, and my heart is dried up; 
\q2 for I have forgotten to eat my bread. 
\q1
\v 6 Because of the voice of my groaning,
\q2  my bone has clung to my flesh. 
\q1
\v 7 I was like a wilderness pelican; 
\q2  I have become like an night-raven in a ruin. 
\q1 
\v 8 I kept awake, and have become like a solitary sparrow on a roof. 
\q1
\v 9 All the day long my enemies have reproached me; 
\q2 and those who praised me have sworn oaths against me. 
\q1
\v 10 For I have eaten ashes as it were bread, 
\q2 and mingled my drink with weeping; 
\q1
\v 11 because of your anger and your wrath: 
\q2 for you have lifted me up, and dashed me down. 
\q1
\v 12 My days have declined like a shadow; 
\q2 and I am withered like grass. 
\q1
\v 13 But you, Lord, endure forever, 
\q2 and your memorial to generation and generation. 
\q1
\v 14 You will arise, and have mercy upon Zion: 
\q2 for \add it is\add* time to have mercy upon her, 
\q2 for the set time has come. 
\q1
\v 15 For your servants have taken pleasure in her stones, 
\q2 and they will pity her dust. 
\q1
\v 16 So the nations will fear your name, O Lord, 
\q2 and all kings your glory. 
\q1
\v 17 For the Lord will build up Zion, 
\q2 and will appear in his glory. 
\q1
\v 18 He has had regard to the prayer of the lowly, 
\q2 and has not despised their petition. 
\q1
\v 19 Let this be written for another generation; 
\q2 and the people being created will praise the Lord. 
\q1
\v 20 For he has looked out from the height of his sanctuary; 
\q2 the Lord looked upon the earth from heaven; 
\q1
\v 21 to hear the groaning of the fettered ones, 
\q2 to loosen the sons of the slain; 
\q1
\v 22 to proclaim the name of the Lord in Zion, 
\q2 and his praise in Jerusalem; 
\q1
\v 23 when the people are gathered together, 
\q2 and the kings, to serve the Lord. 
\q1
\v 24 He answered him in the way of his strength: 
\q2 Declare to me the fewness of my days. 
\q1
\v 25 Don't take me in half my days: 
\q2 your years \add are\add* \x + \xo 101:25 \xt Heb. 1. 11,13.\x*through all generations. 
\q1
\v 26 In the beginning you, O Lord, laid the foundation of the earth; 
\q2 and the heavens are the works of your hands. 
\q1
\v 27 They will perish, but you remain: 
\q2 and they will all grow old like a garment; 
\q2 and as a cloak will you change them, 
\q2 and they will be changed. 
\q1
\v 28 But you are the same, and your years will not fail. 
\q1
\v 29 The children of your servants will abide, 
\q2 and their seed will be established forever. 
\c 102 
\d
\v 1 Of David. 
\q1
\v 1b Bless the Lord, O my soul; 
\q2 and all \add that is\add* within me, \add bless\add* his holy name. 
\q1
