\q1
\v 12 As far as the east is from the west, 
\q2 \add so far\add* has he removed our transgressions from us. 
\q1
\v 13 As a father pities children, 
\q2 the Lord pities those who fear him. 
\q1
\v 14 For he knows our frame: 
\q2 remember that we are dust. 
\q1
\v 15 \add As for\add* man, his days are as grass; 
\q2 as a flower of the field, so he will flourish. 
\q1
\v 16 For the wind passes over it, and it will not be; 
\q2 and it will no longer recognise its place. 
\q1
\v 17 But the mercy of the Lord is from age to age upon those who fear him, 
\q2 and his righteousness to children's children; 
\q1
\v 18 to those who keep his covenant, 
\q2 and remember his commandments to do them. 
\q1
\v 19 The Lord has prepared his throne in the heaven; 
\q2 and his kingdom rules over all. 
\q1
\v 20 Bless the Lord, all you his angels, mighty in strength, 
\q2 who perform his bidding, to hear the voice of his words. 
\q1
\v 21 Bless the Lord, all you his powers; 
\q2 \add you\add* ministers of his that do his will. 
\q1
\v 22 Bless the Lord, all his works, in every place of his dominion: 
\q2 bless the Lord, O my soul. 
\c 103 
\d
\v 1 Of David. 
\q1
\v 1b Bless the Lord, O my soul. 
\q2 O Lord my God, you are very great; 
\q2 you have clothed yourself with praise and splendour: 
\q1
\v 2 who robe yourself with light as with a garment; 
