\q1
\v 12 Then they believed his words, 
\q2 and sang his praise. 
\q1
\v 13 They made haste, they forgot his works; 
\q2 they didn't wait for his counsel. 
\q1
\v 14 They lusted exceedingly in the wilderness, 
\q2 and tempted God in the waterless place.
\q1
\v 15 He gave them their request, 
\q2 and sent fulness into their souls. 
\q1
\v 16 They provoked Moses also in the camp, 
\q2 and Aaron the holy one of the Lord. 
\q1
\v 17 The earth opened and swallowed up Dathan, 
\q2 and closed upon the congregation of Abiram. 
\q1
\v 18 A fire was kindled in their congregation, 
\q2 and a flame burnt up the sinners. 
\q1
\v 19 They made a calf in Horeb, 
\q2 and worshipped the graven image, 
\q1
\v 20 and they exchanged their glory 
\q2 for the likeness of a calf that feeds on grass. 
\q1
\v 21 They forgot God who saved them, 
\q2 who had worked great deeds in Egypt; 
\q1
\v 22 wondrous things in the land of Ham, 
\q2 and fearsome things at the Red Sea. 
\q1
\v 23 So he said that he would have destroyed them, 
\q2 had not Moses his chosen stood before him in the breach, 
\q2 to turn \add him\add* away from the fierceness of his anger, 
\q2 so that he should not destroy them. 
\q1
\v 24 Moreover they despise the desirable land, 
\q2 and didn't believe his word. 
\q1
\v 25 They murmured in their tents: 
\q2 they didn't listen to the voice of the Lord. 
\q1
\v 26 So he lifted up his hand against them, 
\q2 to cast them down in the wilderness, 
\q1
\v 27 and to cast down their seed among the nations, 
\q2 and to scatter them in the lands. 
\q1
\v 28 They were joined also to Baal Peor, 
\q2 and ate the sacrifices of the dead. 
\q1
\v 29 And they provoked him with their devices; 
\q2 and destruction was multiplied among them. 
\q1
\v 30 Then Phinehas stood up, and made atonement: 
\q2 and the plague ceased. 
\q1
\v 31 It was counted to him for righteousness, 
\q2 to all generations forever. 
\q1
\v 32 They angered him also at the water of Strife, 
\q2 and Moses was harmed because of them;
\q1
\v 33 for they embittered his spirit, 
\q2 and he gave command with his lips. 
\q1
\v 34 They didn't destroy the nations 
\q2 as the Lord had told them;
\q1
\v 35 but were mingled with the nations, 
\q2 and learned their works. 
\q1
\v 36 They served their graven images; 
\q2 and it became an stumbling block to them. 
\q1
\v 37 They sacrificed their sons and their daughters to devils, 
\q1
\v 38 and shed innocent blood, 
\q2 the blood of their sons and daughters, 
\q2 whom they sacrificed to the idols of Canaan; 
\q2 and the land was defiled by bloodshed, 
\q1
\v 39 and was polluted with their works; 
\q2 and they played the harlot in their schemes. 
\q1
\v 40 So the Lord was very angry with his people, 
\q2 and he abhorred his inheritance. 
\q1
\v 41 He delivered them into the hands of enemies; 
\q2 and those who hated them ruled over them. 
\q1
\v 42 Their enemies oppressed them, 
\q2 and they were brought down under their hands. 
\q1
\v 43 Many times he delivered them; 
\q2 but they provoked him by their counsel, 
\q2 and they were brought low by their iniquities. 
\q1
\v 44 Yet the Lord looked upon their affliction, 
\q2 when he heard their petition. 
\q1
\v 45 He remembered his covenant, 
\q2 and repented according to the multitude of his mercy. 
\q1
\v 46 He caused them to be pitied 
\q2 in the sight of all who carried them captive. 
\q1
\v 47 Save us, O Lord our God, and gather us from among the nations, 
\q2 that we may give thanks to your holy name, 
\q2 that we may glory in your praise. 
\b
\q1
\v 48 Blessed be the Lord God of Israel from everlasting and to everlasting; 
\q2 and all the people will say, So be it, so be it.
\c 106 
\d
\v 1 Alleluia. 
\q1
\v 1b Give thanks to the Lord, for he is good; 
\q2 for his mercy \add endures\add* forever. 
\q1
\v 2 Let them say \add so\add* who have been redeemed by the Lord, 
\q2 whom he has redeemed from the hand of the enemy; 
\q1
\v 3 and gathered them out of the lands, 
\q2 from the east, and west, and north, and \f + \fr 106:3 \ft Clearly one expects `south' here to complete the four cardinal directions, yet the Greek (and the Hebrew from which it is translated) unambiguously says `sea'. In Hebrew ``the sea'' can be used to directionally, generally meaning west towards the Mediterranean; the fact that `west' is already represented here reveals a different way of thinking about directions.\f*sea. 
\q1
\v 4 They wandered in the wilderness in a dry land; 
\q2 they found no way to a city of habitation. 
\q1
\v 5 Hungry and thirsty, 
\q2 their soul fainted in them. 
\q1
\v 6 Then they cried to the Lord in their affliction, 
\q2 and he delivered them out of their distresses. 
\q1
\v 7 He guided them into a straight path, 
\q2 that they might go to a city of habitation. 
\q1
\v 8 Let them acknowledge to the Lord his mercies, 
\q2 and his wonderful works to the children of men. 
\q1
\v 9 For he satisfies the empty soul, 
\q2 and fills the hungry with good things, 
\q1
\v 10 \add even\add* those who sit in darkness and the shadow of death, 
\q2 fettered in poverty and iron; 
\q1
\v 11 because they rebelled against the words of God, 
\q2 and provoked the purpose of the Most High. 
\q1
\v 12 So their heart was brought low with troubles; 
\q2 they were weak, and there was no helper. 
\q1
\v 13 Then they cried to the Lord in their affliction, 
\q2 and he saved them out of their distresses. 
\q1
\v 14 He brought them out of darkness and the shadow of death, 
\q2 and broke apart their bonds. 
\q1
\v 15 Let them acknowledge to the Lord his mercies, 
\q2 and his wonders to the children of men. 
\q1
\v 16 For he broke to pieces the bronze gates, 
\q2 and crushed the iron bars. 
\q1
\v 17 He helped them out of the way of their wickedness; 
\q2 for they were brought low because of their iniquities. 
\q1
\v 18 Their soul abhorred all food; 
\q2 and they drew near to the gates of death. 
\q1
\v 19 Then they cried to the Lord in their affliction, 
\q2 and he saved them out of their distresses. 
\q1
\v 20 He sent his word, and healed them, 
\q2 and delivered them out of their destructions. 
\q1
\v 21 Let them acknowledge to the Lord his mercies, 
\q2 and his wonderful works to the children of men. 
\q1
\v 22 Let them offer to him the sacrifice of praise, 
\q2 and proclaim his works with exultation. 
\q1
\v 23 Those who go down to the sea in ships, 
\q2 doing business in many waters; 
\q1
\v 24 these have seen the works of the Lord, 
\q2 and his wonders in the deep. 
\q1
\v 25 He speaks, and the stormy wind arises, 
\q2 and its waves are lifted up. 
\q1
\v 26 They go up to the heavens, 
\q2 and go down to the depths; 
\q2 their soul melts because of troubles. 
\q1
\v 27 They are troubled, 
\q2 they stagger as a drunkard, 
\q2 and all their wisdom is swallowed up. 
\q1
\v 28 Then they cry to the Lord in their affliction, 
\q2 and he brings them out of their distresses. 
\q1
\v 29 He commands the storm, 
\q2 and it is calmed into a gentle breeze, 
\q2 and its waves are still. 
\q1
\v 30 They are glad, because they are quiet; 
\q2 and he guides them to their desired haven. 
\q1
\v 31 Let them acknowledge to the Lord his mercies, 
\q2 and his wonderful works to the children of men. 
\q1
\v 32 Let them exalt him in the congregation of the people, 
\q2 and praise him in the seat of the elders. 
\q1
\v 33 He turns rivers into a desert, 
\q2 and streams of water into thirst; 
\q1
\v 34 a fruitful land into salt land, 
\q2 for the wickedness of those who dwell in it. 
\q1
\v 35 He turns a wilderness into pools of water, 
\q2 and a dry land into streams of water. 
\q1
\v 36 There he causes the hungry to dwell, 
\q2 and they establish for themselves a city to dwell in.
\q1
\v 37 They sow fields, and plant vineyards, 
\q2 and they yield fruit of increase. 
\q1
\v 38 He blesses them, and they multiply exceedingly, 
\q2 and he doesn't diminish the number of their cattle. 
\q1
\v 39 Again they become few, and are brought low, 
\q2 by the pressure of evils and pain. 
\q1
\v 40 Contempt is poured upon their princes, 
\q2 and he causes them to wander in a desert and trackless land. 
\q1
\v 41 But he helps the poor man out of poverty, 
\q2 and makes his families like a flock. 
\q1
\v 42 The upright will see and rejoice; 
\q2 and all wickedness will shut its mouth. 
\q1
\v 43 Who is wise, and will observe these things, 
\q2 and understand the mercies of the Lord? 
\c 107 
\d
\v 1 Song of a Psalm. Of David. 
\q1
\v 2 O God, my heart is ready, my heart is ready; 
\q2 I will sing and make melody with my glory. 
\q1
\v 3 Awake, psaltery and harp; 
\q2 I will awake early. 
\q1
\v 4 I will give thanks to you, O Lord, among the people; 
\q2 I will sing praise to you among the nations. 
\q1
\v 5 For your mercy is great above the heavens, 
\q2 and your truth to the clouds. 
\q1
\v 6 Be exalted, O God, above the heavens; 
\q2 and your glory above all the earth. 
\q1
\v 7 That your beloved ones may be delivered, 
\q2 save with your right hand, and hear me. 
\q1 God has spoken in his sanctuary; 
\q1
\v 8 I will be exalted, and will divide Sicima, 
\q2 and will measure out the valley of tents. 
\q1
\v 9 Gilead is mine; and Manasseh is mine; 
\q2 and Ephraim is the help of my head; Judah is my king; 
\q1
\v 10 Moab is the caldron of my hope; 
\q2 over Idumea will I cast my sandal; 
\q2 the Philistines are made subject to me. 
\q1
\v 11 Who will bring me into the fortified city? 
\q2 Or who will guide me to Idumea? 
\q1
\v 12 Will not you, O God, who have rejected us? 
\q2 And will not you, O God, go forth with our hosts? 
\q1
\v 13 Give us help from tribulation: 
\q2 for vain is the help of man. 
\q1
\v 14 Through God we will do mighty deeds; 
\q2 and he will bring to nothing our enemies. 
\c 108 
\d
\v 1 For the end. A Psalm of David.
\q1
\v 1b O God, pass not over my praise in silence; 
\q1
\v 2 for the mouth of the sinner and the mouth of the deceitful \add man\add* have been opened against me:
\q2 they have spoken against me with a deceitful tongue. 
\q1
\v 3 They have surrounded me with words of hatred; 
\q2 and fought against me without a cause. 
\q1
\v 4 \f + \fr 108:4 \fqa Or, \ft instead of loving me.\f*In return for my love, they falsely accused me: 
\q2 but I continued to pray. 
\q1
\v 5 They rewarded me evil for good, 
\q2 and hatred for my love. 
\q1
\v 6 Set a sinner against him; 
\q2 and let an accuser stand at his right hand. 
\q1
\v 7 When he is judged, let him go forth condemned: 
\q2 and let his prayer become guilt. 
\q1
\v 8 Let his days be few: 
\q2 and \x + \xo 108:8 \xt Acts 1. 20.\x*let another take his office. 
\q1
\v 9 Let his children be orphans, 
\q2 and his wife a widow. 
\q1
\v 10 Let his children wander without a dwelling-place, and beg: 
\q2 let them be cast out of their habitations. 
\q1
\v 11 Let a creditor seize all that belongs to him: 
\q2 and let strangers plunder his labours. 
\q1
\v 12 Let him have no helper; 
\q2 neither let there be any one to have compassion on his fatherless children. 
\q1
\v 13 Let his children be for utter destruction: 
\q2 in one generation let his name be blotted out. 
\q1
\v 14 Let the wickedness of his fathers be remembered before the Lord; 
\q2 and don't let the sin of his mother be blotted out. 
\q1
\v 15 Let them be before the Lord continually; 
\q2 and let their memorial be blotted out from the earth. 
\q1
\v 16 Because he didn't remember to show mercy, 
\q2 but persecuted the needy and poor man, 
\q2 and the broken in the heart, to kill him. 
\q1
\v 17 He loved cursing also, and it will come upon him; 
\q2 and he didn't take pleasure in blessing, so it will be removed far from him. 
\q1
\v 18 Yes, he put on cursing as a garment, 
\q2 and it entered as water into his inward parts, 
\q2 and as oil into his bones. 
\q1
\v 19 Let it be to him as a garment which he puts on, 
\q2 and as a belt with which he girds himself continually. 
\q1
\v 20 This is the dealing of the Lord with those who falsely accuse me, 
\q2 and of those who speak evil against my soul. 
\q1
\v 21 But you, O Lord, Lord, deal with me in mercy, for your name's sake: 
\q2 for your mercy is kind. 
\q1
\v 22 Deliver me, for I am poor and needy; 
\q2 and my heart is troubled within me. 
\q1
\v 23 I vanish like a shadow when it declines: 
\q2 I am driven away like locusts. 
\q1
\v 24 My knees are weakened through fasting, 
\q2 and my flesh has wasted away \add lack of\add* oil. 
\q1
\v 25 I became also a reproach to them: 
\q2 they saw me, they shook their heads. 
\q1
\v 26 Help me, O Lord my God; 
\q2 and save me according to your mercy. 
\q1
\v 27 Let them know that this is your hand; 
\q2 and you, Lord, have worked it. 
\q1
\v 28 Let them curse, but you will bless: 
\q2 let those who rise up against me be ashamed, but let your servant rejoice. 
\q1
\v 29 Let those who falsely accuse me be clothed with shame, 
\q2 and let them cover themselves with their shame as with a mantle. 
\q1
\v 30 I will give great thanks to the Lord with my mouth; 
\q2 and among many I will praise him. 
\q1
\v 31 For he stood on the right hand of the poor, 
\q2 to save from those who persecute my soul. 
\c 109 
\d
\v 1 A Psalm of David. 
\q1
\v 1b \x + \xo 109:1 \xt Mat. 22. 44.\x*The Lord said to my Lord, Sit at my right hand, 
\q2 until I make your enemies your footstool. 
\q1
\v 2 The Lord will send forth the rod of your power out of Zion: 
\q2 rule among your enemies. 
\q1
\v 3 With you is dominion in the day of your power, 
\q2 in the splendours of \f + \fr 109:3 \fqa Or, \ft holiness, \fqa i. e. \ft holy things.\f*your saints: 
\q2 I have begotten you from the womb before the morning star. 
\q1
\v 4 The Lord swore, and will not repent, 
\q2 You are a priest forever, after the order of Melchizedek. 
\q1
\v 5 The Lord at your right hand 
\q2 has shattered kings in the day of his wrath. 
\q1
\v 6 He will judge among the nations, 
\q2 he will fill with corpses, 
\q2 he will crush heads over all the earth. 
\q1
\v 7 He will drink of the brook in the way; 
\q2 therefore he will lift up the head. 
\c 110 
\d
\v 1 Alleluia.
\q1 I will give you thanks, O Lord, with my whole heart, 
\q2 in the council of the upright, 
\q2 and \add in\add* the congregation. 
\q1
\v 2 The works of the Lord are great, 
\q2 sought out according to all his will. 
\q1
\v 3 Thanksgiving and majesty are his work: 
\q2 and his righteousness endures forever and ever. 
\q1
\v 4 He has caused his wonderful works to be remembered: 
\q2 the Lord is merciful and compassionate. 
\q1
\v 5 He has given food to those who fear him: 
\q2 he will remember his covenant forever. 
\q1
\v 6 He has declared to his people the power of his works, 
\q2 to give them the inheritance of the nations. 
\q1
\v 7 The works of his hands are truth and justice: 
\q2 all his commandments are faithful: 
\q1
\v 8 established forever and ever, 
\q2 done in truth and uprightness. 
\q1
\v 9 He sent redemption to his people: 
\q2 he commanded his covenant forever: 
\q2 holy and fearsome is his name. 
\q1
\v 10 The fear of the Lord is the \f + \fr 110:10 \fqa Or, \ft sum.\f*beginning of wisdom, 
\q2 and all who act accordingly have a good understanding; 
\q2 his praise endures forever and ever. 
\c 111 
\d
\v 1 Alleluia. 
\q1 Blessed is the man who fears the Lord:
\q2 he will delight greatly in his commandments. 
\q1
\v 2 His seed will be mighty in the earth: 
\q2 the generation of the upright will be blessed. 
\q1
\v 3 Glory and riches will be in his house; 
\q2 and his righteousness endures for evermore. 
\q1
\v 4 To the upright light has sprung up in darkness: 
\q2 he is merciful, and compassionate, and righteous. 
\q1
\v 5 The good man is he who pities and lends: 
\q2 he will direct his affairs with justice. 
\q1
\v 6 For he will not be moved forever; 
\q2 the righteous will be in everlasting remembrance. 
\q1
\v 7 He will not be afraid of an evil report: 
\q2 his heart is ready to trust in the Lord. 
\q1
\v 8 His heart is established, he will not fear, 
\q2 till he looks upon his enemies. 
\q1
\v 9 \x + \xo 111:9 \xt 2 Cor. 9. 9.\x*He has dispersed abroad; he has given to the poor; 
\q2 his righteousness endures for evermore: his horn will be exalted with honour. 
\q1
\v 10 The sinner will see and be angry, he will gnash his teeth, and waste away: 
\q2 the desire of the sinners will perish. 
\c 112 
\d
\v 1 Alleluia. 
\q1 Praise the Lord, you children,
\q2 praise the name of the Lord. 
\q1
\v 2 Let the name of the Lord be blessed, 
\q2 now and forever. 
\q1
\v 3 From the rising of the sun to his setting, 
\q2 praise the name of the Lord.
\q1
\v 4 The Lord is high above all the nations; 
\q2 his glory is above the heavens. 
\q1
\v 5 Who is like the Lord our God? 
\q2 Who dwells in the high places, 
\q1
\v 6 and looks upon the lowly things
\q2 in heaven and on earth: 
\q1
\v 7 who lifts up the poor from the earth, 
\q2 and raises up the needy from the dunghill; 
\q1
\v 8 to set him with princes, 
\q2 with the princes of his people: 
\q1
\v 9 who settles the barren woman in a house, 
\q2 a mother rejoicing over children. 
\c 113 
\d
\v 1 Alleluia. 
\q1
\v 1b When Israel went out from Egypt, 
\q2 of the house of Jacob from a foreign people, 
\q1
\v 2 Judah became his \f + \fr 113:2 \fqa Or, \ft consecrated thing.\f*sanctuary, 
\q2 Israel his dominion. 
\q1
\v 3 The sea saw and fled: 
\q2 Jordan was turned back. 
\q1
\v 4 The mountains skipped like rams, 
\q2 and the hills like lambs. 
\q1
\v 5 What ailed you, O sea, that you fled? 
\q2 And you Jordan, that you were turned back? 
\q1
\v 6 You mountains, that you skipped like rams, 
\q2 and you hills, like lambs? 
\q1
\v 7 The earth trembled at the presence of the Lord, 
\q2 at the presence of the God of Jacob; 
\q1
\v 8 who turned the rock into pools of water, 
\q2 and the sharp rock into fountains of water. 
\q1
\v 9 \f + \fr 113:9 \ft The Greek numbering and division of these psalms differs from the Hebrew.\f*Not to us, O Lord, not to us, but to your name give glory, 
\q2 because of your mercy and your truth; 
\q1
\v 10 lest at any time the nations should say, 
\q2 Where is their God? 
\q1
\v 11 But our God has done in heaven and on earth, 
\q2 whatever he has pleased. 
\q1
\v 12 The idols of the nations are silver and gold, 
\q2 the works of men's hands. 
\q1
\v 13 They have a mouth, but will not speak; 
\q2 they have eyes, but will not see: 
\q1
\v 14 they have ears, but will not hear; 
\q2 they have noses, but will not smell; 
\q1
\v 15 they have hands, but will not feel; 
\q2 they have feet, but will not walk: 
\q2 they will make no sound in their throat. 
\q1
\v 16 Let those that make them become like to them, 
\q2 and all who trust in them. 
\q1
\v 17 The house of Israel hoped in the Lord: 
\q2 he is their helper and defender. 
\q1
\v 18 The house of Aaron hoped in the Lord: 
\q2 he is their helper and defender. 
\q1
\v 19 Those who fear the Lord hoped in the Lord: 
\q2 he is their helper and defender. 
\q1
\v 20 The Lord has remembered us, and blessed us: 
\q2 he has blessed the house of Israel, he has blessed the house of Aaron. 
\q1
\v 21 He has blessed those who fear the Lord, 
\q2 both small and great. 
\q1
\v 22 The Lord increase you,
\q2 you and your children. 
\q1
\v 23 Blessed are you of the Lord, 
\q2 who made the heaven and the earth. 
\q1
\v 24 The heaven of \f + \fr 113:24 \fqa Gr. \ft sing.\f*heavens belongs to the Lord: 
\q2 but he has given the earth to the sons of men. 
\q1
\v 25 The dead will not praise you, O Lord, 
\q2 nor any that go down to Hades. 
\q1
\v 26 But we, the living, will bless the Lord, 
\q2 now and forever. 
\c 114 
\d
\v 1 Alleluia. 
\q1
\v 1b I love, because the Lord will hear the voice of my supplication. 
\q1
\v 2 Because he has inclined his ear to me, 
\q2 and in my days I will call upon him. 
\q1
\v 3 The pangs of death surrounded me; 
\q2 the dangers of Hades found me: 
\q2 I found affliction and sorrow. 
\q1
\v 4 Then I called on the name of the Lord: 
\q2 O Lord, deliver my soul. 
\q1
\v 5 The Lord is merciful and righteous; 
\q2 yes, our God shows mercy. 
\q1
\v 6 The Lord preserves infants: 
\q2 I was brought low, and he delivered me. 
\q1
\v 7 Return to your rest, O my soul; 
\q2 for the Lord has dealt kindly with you. 
\q1
\v 8 For he has delivered my soul from death, 
\q2 my eyes from tears, and my feet from falling. 
\q1
\v 9 I will be pleasing before the Lord in the land of the living.
\b
\c 115 
\d
\v 1 \f + \fr 115:1 \ft The Greek numbering and division of these psalms differs from the Hebrew.\f*Alleluia. 
\q1
\v 1b \x + \xo 115:1 \xt 2 Cor. 4. 13.\x*I believed, therefore I spoke:
\q2 but I was greatly afflicted. 
\q1
\v 2 I said in my amazement,
\q2 Every man is a liar. 
\q1
\v 3 What will I give to the Lord
\q2 for all the things with which he has rewarded me? 
\q1
\v 4 I will take the cup of salvation,
\q2 and call upon the name of the Lord. 
\q1
\v 5 \f + \fr 115:5 \ft This verse is absent in some Greek copies; Rahlfs excludes it from his main text but includes it in the apparatus.\f*I will pay my vows to the Lord,
\q2 in the presence of all his people. 
\q1
\v 6 Precious in the sight of the Lord is the death of his saints. 
\q1
\v 7 O Lord, I am your servant;
\q2 I am your servant, and the son of your handmaid:
\q2 you have burst my bonds asunder. 
\q1
\v 8 I will offer you the sacrifice of praise,
\q2 and will call upon the name of the Lord. 
\q1
\v 9 I will pay my vows to the Lord,
\q2 in the presence of all his people, 
\q1
\v 10 in the courts of the Lord's house,
\q2 in your midst, O Jerusalem. 
\c 116 
\d
\v 1 Alleluia. 
\q1
\v 1b \x + \xo 116:1 \xt Rom. 15. 11.\x* Praise the Lord, all you nations:
\q2 praise him, all you peoples. 
\q1
\v 2 For his mercy has been abundant toward us:
\q2 and the truth of the Lord endures forever. 
\c 117 
\d
\v 1 Alleluia. 
\q1
\v 1b Give thanks to the Lord; for he is good:
\q2 for his mercy is forever. 
\q1
\v 2 Let now the house of Israel say, that he is good: 
\q2 for his mercy is forever. 
\q1
\v 3 Let now the house of Aaron say, that he is good: 
\q2 for his mercy is forever. 
\q1
\v 4 Let now all who fear the Lord say, that he is good: 
\q2 for his mercy is forever. 
\q1
\v 5 From constraint I called on the Lord: 
\q2 and he answered me with spaciousness. 
\q1
\v 6 \x + \xo 117:6 \xt Heb. 13. 6.\x*The Lord is my helper; 
\q2 and I will not fear what man will do to me. 
\q1
\v 7 The Lord is my helper; 
\q2 and I will look upon my enemies. 
\q1
\v 8 Better to trust in the Lord than to trust in man. 
\q1
\v 9 Better to hope in the Lord than to hope in princes. 
\q1
\v 10 All nations surrounded me: 
\q2 but in the name of the Lord I repulsed them. 
\q1
\v 11 They completely surrounded me: 
\q2 but in the name of the Lord I repulsed them. 
\q1
\v 12 They surrounded me as bees do a honeycomb, 
\q2 and they burst into flame as fire among thorns: 
\q2 but in the name of the Lord I repulsed them. 
\q1
\v 13 I was thrust, and overturned, that I might fall: 
\q2 but the Lord helped me. 
\q1
\v 14 The Lord is my strength and my song, 
\q2 and has become my salvation. 
\q1
\v 15 The voice of exultation and salvation is in the tents of the righteous: 
\q2 the right hand of the Lord has worked mightily. 
\q1
\v 16 The right hand of the Lord has exalted me: 
\q2 the right hand of the Lord has worked powerfully. 
\q1
\v 17 I will not die, but live, 
\q2 and recount the works of the Lord. 
\q1
\v 18 The Lord has chastened me severely: 
\q2 but he has not given me up to death. 
\q1
\v 19 Open to me the gates of righteousness: 
\q2 I will go into them, and give praise to the Lord. 
\q1
\v 20 This is the gate of the Lord: 
\q2 the righteous will enter by it. 
\q1
\v 21 I will give thanks to you; 
\q2 because you have heard me, 
\q2 and have become my salvation. 
\q1
\v 22 \x + \xo 117:22 \xt Mat. 21. 42.\x*The stone which the builders rejected, 
\q2 this has become the head of the corner. 
\q1
\v 23 This has been done by the Lord; 
\q2 and it is wonderful in our eyes. 
\q1
\v 24 This is the day which the Lord has made: 
\q2 let us exult and rejoice in it. 
\q1
\v 25 O Lord, save now: 
\q2 O Lord, prosper us now. 
\q1
\v 26 \x + \xo 117:26 \xt Mat. 21. 9.\x*Blessed is he who comes in the name of the Lord: 
\q2 we have blessed you out of the house of the Lord. 
\q1
\v 27 God is the Lord, and he has shone upon us: 
\q2 celebrate the feast with thick \add branches\add*,
\q2 even to the horns of the altar. 
\q1
\v 28 You are my God, and I will give you thanks: 
\q2 you are my God, and I will exalt you. 
\q2 I will give thanks to you, for you have heard me, 
\q2 and have become my salvation. 
\q1
\v 29 Give thanks to the Lord; for he is good: 
\q2 for his mercy is forever. 
\c 118 
\d
\v 1 Alleluia.
\d
\v 1b \f + \fr 118:1 \ft Some Greek copies include the names of the Hebrew letters in this acrostic psalm; others do not. Rahlfs includes them in the main text, but Brenton does not.\f*Aleph
\q1 Blessed are the blameless in the way, 
\q2 who walk in the law of the Lord. 
\q1
\v 2 Blessed are those who search out his testimonies: 
\q2 they will diligently seek him with the whole heart. 
\q1
\v 3 For those who work lawlessness have not walked in his ways. 
\q1
\v 4 You have commanded your commandments to be diligently kept.
\q1
\v 5 O that my ways were directed to keep your ordinances. 
\q1
\v 6 Then I will not be ashamed, 
\q2 when I have respect to all your commandments. 
\q1
\v 7 I will give you thanks with uprightness of heart,
\q2  when I have learnt the judgments of your righteousness. 
\q1
\v 8 I will keep your ordinances: 
\q2 O don't utterly forsake me.
\d Beth
\q1
\v 9 With what will a young man direct his way? 
\q2 By keeping your words. 
\q1
\v 10 With my whole heart have I diligently sought you: 
\q2 don't cast me away from your commandments. 
\q1
\v 11 I have hidden your oracles in my heart, 
\q2 that I might not sin against you. 
\q1
\v 12 You are blessed, O Lord:
\q2 teach me your ordinances. 
\q1
\v 13 With my lips have I declared all the judgments of your mouth. 
\q1
\v 14 I have delighted in the way of your testimonies, 
\q2 as in all riches. 
\q1
\v 15 I will meditate on your commandments, 
\q2 and consider your ways. 
\q1
\v 16 I will meditate on your ordinances: 
\q2 I will not forget your words.
\d Gimel
\q1
\v 17 Give recompense to your servant: 
\q2 I will live, and keep your words. 
\q1
\v 18 Unveil my eyes, 
\q2 and I will perceive your wonders from your law. 
\q1
\v 19 I am a stranger on the earth: 
\q2 don't hide your commandments from me. 
\q1
\v 20 My soul has yearned with longing for your judgments at all times. 
\q1
\v 21 You have rebuked the proud: 
\q2 cursed are those who turn aside from your commandments. 
\q1
\v 22 Remove from me reproach and contempt; 
\q2 for I have sought out your testimonies. 
\q1
\v 23 For princes sat and spoke against me: 
\q2 but your servant was meditating on your ordinances. 
\q1
\v 24 For your testimonies are my meditation, 
\q2 and your ordinances are my counsellors. 
\d Daleth
\q1
\v 25 My soul clung to the ground; 
\q2 revive me according to your word. 
\q1
\v 26 I declared my ways, and you heard me; 
\q2 teach me your ordinances. 
\q1
\v 27 Instruct me in the way of your ordinances; 
\q2 and I will meditate on your wondrous works. 
\q1
\v 28 My soul has melted away from despondency;
\q2 strengthen me with your words. 
\q1
\v 29 Remove from me the way of wickedness; 
\q2 and be merciful to me by your law. 
\q1
\v 30 I have chosen the way of truth; 
\q2 and have not forgotten your judgments. 
\q1
\v 31 I have clung to your testimonies, 
\q2 O Lord; don't put me to shame. 
\q1
\v 32 I ran the way of your commandments, 
\q2 when you enlarged my heart. 
\d He
\q1
\v 33 Lay down for me, O Lord, the way of your ordinances, 
\q2 and I will seek it out continually. 
\q1
\v 34 Instruct me, and I will search out your law, 
\q2 and will keep it with my whole heart. 
\q1
\v 35 Guide me in the path of your commandments; 
\q2 for I have desired it. 
\q1
\v 36 Incline my heart to your testimonies, 
\q2 and not to covetousness. 
\q1
\v 37 Turn away my eyes that I may not behold vanity: 
\q2 revive me in your way. 
\q1
\v 38 Confirm your oracle to your servant for the fear of you. 
\q1
\v 39 Take away my reproach which I have feared: 
\q2 for your judgments are good. 
\q1
\v 40 Behold, I have desired your commandments: 
\q2 revive me in your righteousness. 
\d Waw
\q1
\v 41 Let your mercy come upon me, O Lord; 
\q2 your salvation, according to your word. 
\q1
\v 42 Then I will answer those who reproach me with a word: 
\q2 for I have trusted in your words. 
\q1
\v 43 Don't take the word of truth completely out of my mouth; 
\q2 for I have hoped in your judgments. 
\q1
\v 44 So I will keep your law continually, 
\q2 forever and ever. 
\q1
\v 45 I walked in spaciousness: 
\q2 for I sought out your commandments. 
\q1
\v 46 I spoke of your testimonies before kings, 
\q2 and was not ashamed. 
\q1
\v 47 I would meditate on your commandments, 
\q2 which I loved exceedingly. 
\q1
\v 48 I lifted up my hands to your commandments which I loved; 
\q2 and I meditated on your ordinances. 
\d Zayin
\q1
\v 49 Remember your word to your servant, 
\q2 in which you made me hope. 
\q1
\v 50 This has comforted me in my affliction: 
\q2 for your oracle has revived me. 
\q1
\v 51 The proud have transgressed exceedingly; 
\q2 but I didn't swerve from your law. 
\q1
\v 52 I remembered your judgments of old, O Lord;
\q2 and was comforted. 
\q1
\v 53 Despair took hold upon me, 
\q2 because of the sinners who forsake your law. 
\q1
\v 54 Your ordinances were my songs in the place of my sojourning. 
\q1
\v 55 I remembered your name, O Lord, in the night, 
\q2 and kept your law. 
\q1
\v 56 This was mine because I diligently sought your ordinances. 
\d Heth
\q1
\v 57 You are my portion, O Lord: 
\q2 I said that I would keep your law. 
\q1
\v 58 I sought your face with my whole heart: 
\q2 have mercy upon me according to your word. 
\q1
\v 59 I thought on your ways, 
\q2 and turned my feet to your testimonies. 
\q1
\v 60 I prepared myself and was not troubled
\q2 to keep your commandments. 
\q1
\v 61 The cords of sinners entangled me: 
\q2 but I didn't forget your law. 
\q1
\v 62 At midnight I arose, 
\q2 to give thanks to you for the judgments of your righteousness. 
\q1
\v 63 I am a companion of all those who fear you, 
\q2 and of those who keep your commandments. 
\q1
\v 64 O Lord, the earth is full of your mercy: 
\q2 teach me your ordinances. 
\d Teth
\q1
\v 65 You have dealt kindly with your servant, O Lord, 
\q2 according to your word. 
\q1
\v 66 Teach me goodness, and instruction, and knowledge: 
\q2 for I have believed your commandments. 
\q1
\v 67 Before I was afflicted, I transgressed; 
\q2 therefore have I kept your word. 
\q1
\v 68 You are good, O Lord; 
\q2 in your goodness teach me your ordinances. 
\q1
\v 69 The injustice of the proud has been multiplied against me: 
\q2 but I will search out your commandments with all my heart. 
\q1
\v 70 Their heart has been curdled like milk; 
\q2 but I have meditated on your law. 
\q1
\v 71 It is good for me that you have humbled me; 
\q2 that I might learn your ordinances. 
\q1
\v 72 The law of your mouth is better to me than thousands of gold and silver. 
\d Yodh
\q1
\v 73 Your hands have made me, and fashioned me: 
\q2 instruct me, that I may learn your commandments. 
\q1
\v 74 Those who fear you will see me and rejoice: 
\q2 for I have hoped in your words. 
\q1
\v 75 I know, O Lord, that your judgments are righteousness, 
\q2 and in truthfulness you have humbled me. 
\q1
\v 76 Please let your mercy be for my comfort, 
\q2 according to your word to your servant. 
\q1
\v 77 Let your compassions come to me, that I may live: 
\q2 for your law is my meditation. 
\q1
\v 78 Let the proud be ashamed; for they transgressed against me unjustly: 
\q2 but I will meditate on your commandments. 
\q1
\v 79 Let those who fear you, 
\q2 and those who know your testimonies, turn to me. 
\q1
\v 80 Let my heart be blameless in your ordinances, 
\q2 that I may not be ashamed. 
\d Kaph
\q1
\v 81 My soul faints for your salvation: 
\q2 I have hoped in your words. 
\q1
\v 82 My eyes failed waiting for your word, 
\q2 saying, When will you comfort me? 
\q1
\v 83 For I have become as a wineskin in the frost: 
\q2 I have not forgotten your ordinances. 
\q1
\v 84 How many are the days of your servant? 
\q2 When will you execute judgment for me on those who persecute me? 
\q1
\v 85 Transgressors told me idle tales; 
\q2 but not according to your law, O Lord. 
\q1
\v 86 All your commandments are truth; 
\q2 they persecuted me unjustly: help me. 
\q1
\v 87 They nearly made an end of me on the earth; 
\q2 but I didn't forsake your commandments. 
\q1
\v 88 Revive me according to your mercy; 
\q2 so I will keep the testimonies of your mouth. 
\d Lamedh
\q1
\v 89 Forever, O Lord, your word abides in heaven. 
\q1
\v 90 Your truth is to all generations; 
\q2 you have founded the earth, and it abides. 
\q1
\v 91 The day continues by your ordinance; 
\q2 for all things are your servants. 
\q1
\v 92 If your law was not my meditation, 
\q2 then I would have perished in my humiliation. 
\q1
\v 93 I will never forget your ordinances; 
\q2 for with them you have revived me. 
\q1
\v 94 I am yours, save me; 
\q2 for I have sought out your ordinances. 
\q1
\v 95 Sinners waited for me to destroy me; 
\q2 I understood your testimonies. 
\q1
\v 96 I have seen the limit of every completion; 
\q2 your commandment is very broad. 
\d Mem
\q1
\v 97 How I have loved your law, O Lord! 
\q2 It is my meditation all day long. 
\q1
\v 98 Your commandment has made me wiser than my enemies;
\q2 for it is mine forever. 
\q1
\v 99 I have more understanding than all my teachers; 
\q2 for your testimonies are my meditation. 
\q1
\v 100 I understand more than the aged; 
\q2 because I have sought out your commandments. 
\q1
\v 101 I have kept back my feet from every evil way, 
\q2 that I might keep your words. 
\q1
\v 102 I have not declined from your judgments; 
\q2 for you have \f + \fr 118:102 \ft That is, as a lawgiver.\f*instructed me. 
\q1
\v 103 How sweet are your oracles to my throat! 
\q2 More so than honey to my mouth! 
\q1
\v 104 I gain understanding by your commandments: 
\q2 therefore I have hated every way of unrighteousness. 
\d Nun
\q1
\v 105 Your word is a lamp to my feet, 
\q2 and a light to my paths. 
\q1
\v 106 I have sworn and determined to keep the judgments of your righteousness. 
\q1
\v 107 I have been very greatly humbled, O Lord: 
\q2 revive me, according to your word. 
\q1
\v 108 Please accept, O Lord, the freewill-offerings of my mouth, 
\q2 and teach me your judgments. 
\q1
\v 109 My soul is continually in my hands; 
\q2 and I have not forgotten your law. 
\q1
\v 110 Sinners spread a snare for me; 
\q2 but I didn't stray from your commandments. 
\q1
\v 111 I have inherited your testimonies forever; 
\q2 for they are the joy of my heart. 
\q1
\v 112 I have inclined my heart to perform your ordinances forever, for recompense. 
\d Samekh
\q1
\v 113 I have hated transgressors; 
\q2 but I have loved your law. 
\q1
\v 114 You are my helper and my defender; 
\q2 I have hoped in your words. 
\q1
\v 115 Depart from me, you evil-doers; 
\q2 and I will search out the commandments of my God. 
\q1
\v 116 Uphold me according to your word, and revive me; 
\q2 and do not put me to shame in my expectation.
\q1
\v 117 Help me, and I will be saved; 
\q2 and I will meditate on your ordinances continually. 
\q1
\v 118 You have brought to nothing all who depart from your ordinances; 
\q2 for their inward thought is unrighteous. 
\q1
\v 119 I have reckoned all the sinners of the earth as transgressors; 
\q2 therefore have I loved your testimonies continually. 
\q1
\v 120 Nail my flesh with your fear;
\q2 for I am afraid of your judgments. 
\d Ayin
\q1
\v 121 I have done justice and righteousness; 
\q2 don't deliver me up to those who wrong me. 
\q1
\v 122 Receive your servant for good: 
\q2 don't let the proud accuse me falsely. 
\q1
\v 123 My eyes have failed for your salvation, 
\q2 and for the word of your righteousness. 
\q1
\v 124 Deal with your servant according to your mercy, 
\q2 and teach me your ordinances. 
\q1
\v 125 I am your servant; give me understanding, 
\q2 and I will know your testimonies. 
\q1
\v 126 It is time for the Lord to act: 
\q2 they have made void your law. 
\q1
\v 127 Therefore have I loved your commandments
\q2 more than gold and topaz. 
\q1
\v 128 Therefore I was guided aright by all your commandments: 
\q2 I have hated every unjust way. 
\d Pe
\q1
\v 129 Your testimonies are wonderful: 
\q2 therefore my soul has searched them out. 
\q1
\v 130 The unfolding of your words gives light, 
\q2 and instructs little ones. 
\q1
\v 131 I opened my mouth, and drew breath: 
\q2 for I longed for your commandments. 
\q1
\v 132 Look upon me and have mercy upon me, 
\q2 after the manner of those who love your name. 
\q1
\v 133 Order my steps according to your word: 
\q2 and don't let any lawlessness have dominion over me. 
\q1
\v 134 Deliver me from the false accusation of men: 
\q2 so will I keep your commandments. 
\q1
\v 135 Cause your face to shine upon your servant: 
\q2 and teach me your ordinances. 
\q1
\v 136 Streams of water ran down from my eyes, 
\q2 because they didn't keep your law. 
\d Tsade
\q1
\v 137 You are righteous, O Lord, 
\q2 and your judgment is upright. 
\q1
\v 138 You have commanded your testimonies as righteousness and great truth.
\q1
\v 139 Zeal for your house has consumed me: 
\q2 because my enemies have forgotten your words. 
\q1
\v 140 Your word has been thoroughly refined; 
\q2 and your servant loves it. 
\q1
\v 141 I am young and despised: 
\q2 I have not forgotten your ordinances. 
\q1
\v 142 Your righteousness is an everlasting righteousness, 
\q2 and your law is truth. 
\q1
\v 143 Afflictions and distresses found me: 
\q2 your commandments are my meditation. 
\q1
\v 144 Your testimonies are everlasting righteousness: 
\q2 give me understanding, and I will live. 
\d Qoph
\q1
\v 145 I cried with my whole heart; hear me, O Lord: 
\q2 I will search out your ordinances. 
\q1
\v 146 I cried to you; 
\q2 save me, and I will keep your testimonies. 
\q1
\v 147 I arose before the dawn, and cried: 
\q2 I hoped in your words. 
\q1
\v 148 My eyes anticipated the dawn, 
\q2 that I might meditate on your oracles. 
\q1
\v 149 Hear my voice, O Lord, according to your mercy; 
\q2 revive me according to your judgment. 
\q1
\v 150 Those who persecuted me unlawfully have drawn near; 
\q2 and they are far removed from your law. 
\q1
\v 151 You are near, O Lord; 
\q2 and all your commandments are truth. 
\q1
\v 152 Of old I knew from your testimonies, 
\q2 that you have founded them forever. 
\d Resh
\q1
\v 153 Look upon my humiliation, and rescue me; 
\q2 for I have not forgotten your law. 
\q1
\v 154 Plead my cause, and ransom me: 
\q2 revive me because of your word. 
\q1
\v 155 Salvation is far from sinners: 
\q2 for they have not searched out your ordinances. 
\q1
\v 156 Your mercies, O Lord, are many: 
\q2 revive me according to your judgment. 
\q1
\v 157 Many are those who persecute me and oppress me: 
\q2 I have not turned aside from your testimonies. 
\q1
\v 158 I saw the faithless, and I pined away; 
\q2 for they didn't keep your oracles. 
\q1
\v 159 Behold, I have loved your commandments, O Lord: 
\q2 revive me in your mercy. 
\q1
\v 160 The \f + \fr 118:160 \fqa Or, \ft sum.\ft*beginning of your words is truth; 
\q2 and all the judgments of your righteousness are forever. 
\d Sin/Shin
\q1
\v 161 Princes persecuted me without a cause, 
\q2 but my heart feared because of your words. 
\q1
\v 162 I will exult because of your oracles, 
\q2 as one who finds much spoil. 
\q1
\v 163 I hated and abhorred unrighteousness; 
\q2 but I loved your law. 
\q1
\v 164 Seven times a day I have praised you 
\q2 because of the judgments of your righteousness. 
\q1
\v 165 Those who love your law have great peace: 
\q2 and there is no stumbling-block for them. 
\q1
\v 166 I have waited for your salvation, O Lord, 
\q2 and have loved your commandments. 
\q1
\v 167 My soul has kept your testimonies, 
\q2 and loved them exceedingly. 
\q1
\v 168 I have kept your commandments and your testimonies; 
\q2 for all my ways are before you, O Lord. 
\d Tav
\q1
\v 169 Let my supplication come near before you, O Lord; 
\q2 give me understanding according to your oracle. 
\q1
\v 170 Let my petition come in before you, O Lord; 
\q2 deliver me according to your oracle. 
\q1
\v 171 Let my lips pour forth a hymn, 
\q2 when you teach me your ordinances. 
\q1
\v 172 Let my tongue utter your oracles; 
\q2 for all your commandments are righteousness. 
\q1
\v 173 Let your hand be \add ready\add* to save me; 
\q2 for I have chosen your commandments. 
\q1
\v 174 I have longed for your salvation, O Lord; 
\q2 and your law is my meditation. 
\q1
\v 175 My soul will live, and will praise you; 
\q2 and your judgments will help me. 
\q1
\v 176 I have gone astray like a lost sheep; 
\q2 seek your servant; 
\q2 for I have not forgotten your commandments. 
\c 119 
\d
\v 1 A Song of Ascents. 
\q1
\v 1b In my affliction I cried to the Lord,
\q2 and he listened to me. 
\q1
\v 2 Deliver my soul, O Lord, from unjust lips, 
\q2 and from a deceitful tongue. 
\q1
\v 3 What should be given to you, 
\q2 and what should be added to you, O deceitful tongue? 
\q1
\v 4 Sharpened arrows of the mighty, 
\q2 with desert coals.
\q1
\v 5 Woe is me, that my sojourning is prolonged; 
\q2 I have dwelt among the tents of Kedar. 
\q1
\v 6 My soul has long been a sojourner; 
\q1
\v 7 I was peaceable with those who hated peace; 
\q2 when I spoke to them, they warred against me without cause. 
\c 120 
\d
\v 1 A Song of Ascents. 
\q1
\v 1b I lifted up my eyes to the mountains; 
\q2 where will my help come from? 
\q1
\v 2 My help is from the Lord,
\q2 who made the heaven and the earth. 
\q1
\v 3 May he not let your foot be shaken; 
\q2 and may the one who keeps you not slumber. 
\q1
\v 4 Behold, he who keeps Israel will not slumber nor sleep. 
\q1
\v 5 The Lord will keep you: 
\q2 the Lord is your shelter at your right hand. 
\q1
\v 6 The sun will not scorch you by day, 
\q2 nor the moon by night. 
\q1
\v 7 The Lord will keep you from every evil: 
\q2 he will keep your soul. 
\q1
\v 8 The Lord will keep your coming in and your going out, 
\q2 from now on and forever. 
\c 121 
\d
\v 1 A Song of Ascents.
\q1
\v 1b I was glad when they said to me, 
\q2 Let us go into the house of the Lord. 
\q1
\v 2 Our feet are standing in your courts, O Jerusalem. 
\q1
\v 3 Jerusalem is built as a city
\q2 joined together into one. 
\q1
\v 4 For there the tribes went up, 
\q2 the tribes of the Lord, as a testimony for Israel, 
\q2 to give thanks to the name of the Lord. 
\q1
\v 5 For there are set thrones for judgment, 
\q2 thrones for the house of David. 
\q1
\v 6 \f + \fr 121:6 \fqa Or, \ft ask Jerusalem how it is with her.\f*Pray now for the peace of Jerusalem: 
\q2 and prosperity to those who love you. 
\q1
\v 7 Let peace, I pray, be within your strengths, 
\q2 and prosperity in your strongholds. 
\q1
\v 8 For the sake of my brothers and my neighbours, 
\q2 I indeed spoke peace concerning you. 
\q1
\v 9 Because of the house of the Lord our God, 
\q2 I have diligently sought your good. 
\c 122 
\d
\v 1 A Song of Ascents. 
\q1
\v 1b To you who dwell in heaven I have lifted up my eyes. 
\q1
\v 2 Behold, as the eyes of servants are to the hands of their masters, 
\q2 as the eyes of a maiden-servant to the hands of her mistress; 
\q2 so our eyes are to the Lord our God, until he has mercy upon us. 
\q1
\v 3 Have pity upon us, O Lord, have pity upon us: 
\q2 for we are exceedingly filled with contempt. 
\q1
\v 4 Our soul has been filled exceedingly 
\q2 with the reproach of those who are at ease, 
\q2 and with contempt from the proud. 
\c 123 
\d
\v 1 A Song of Ascents. 
\q1
\v 1b If it had not been that the Lord was among us, 
\q2 let Israel now say; 
\q1
\v 2 if it had not been that the Lord was among us, 
\q2 when men rose up against us; 
\q1
\v 3 then they would have swallowed us up alive, 
\q2 when their wrath was kindled against us: 
\q1
\v 4 then the water would have drowned us, 
\q2 our soul would have gone under the torrent. 
\q1
\v 5 Yes, our soul would have gone under the overwhelming water. 
\q1
\v 6 Blessed be the Lord, 
\q2 who has not given us as prey to their teeth. 
\q1
\v 7 Our soul has been delivered as a sparrow from the snare of the hunters: 
\q2 the snare is broken, and we are delivered. 
\q1
\v 8 Our help is in the name of the Lord, 
\q2 who made heaven and earth. 
\c 124 
\d
\v 1 A Song of Ascents.
\q1
\v 1b Those who trust in the Lord are as mount Zion: 
\q2 the one who dwells in Jerusalem will never be moved. 
\q1
\v 2 The mountains are all around her, 
\q2 and the Lord is all around his people, 
\q2 from now on and forever. 
\q1
\v 3 For the Lord will not allow the rod of sinners to be upon the lot of the righteous; 
\q2 lest the righteous should stretch forth their hands to wickedness. 
\q1
\v 4 Do good, O Lord, to the good, and to the upright in heart. 
\q1
\v 5 But those who turn aside into crooked ways
\q2 the Lord will lead away
\q2 with the workers of lawlessness. 
\q1 Peace be upon Israel. 
\c 125 
\d
\v 1 A Song of Ascents. 
\q1
\v 1b When the Lord turned the captivity of Zion, we were like those who are comforted. 
\q1
\v 2 Then was our mouth filled with joy, and our tongue with exultation: 
\q2 then they will say among the nations,
\q2 The Lord has done great things with them. 
\q1
\v 3 The Lord has done great things with us;
\q2 we became joyful. 
\q1
\v 4 Turn, O Lord, our captivity,
\q2 as the torrents in the south. 
\q1
\v 5 Those who sow in tears will reap in joy. 
\q1
\v 6 Going, they went and wept, carrying their seeds; 
\q2 but coming, they will come with exultation, carrying their sheaves.
\c 126 
\d
\v 1 A Song of Ascents. Of Solomon.
\q1
\v 1b Unless the Lord builds the house, those who build labour in vain:
\q2 unless the Lord keeps the city, the watchman watches in vain. 
\q1
\v 2 It is vain for you to rise early: 
\q2 to sit up late, eating the bread of grief; 
\q2 when he gives sleep to his beloved. 
\q1
\v 3 Behold, children are the inheritance of the Lord, 
\q2 the reward of the fruit of the womb. 
\q1
\v 4 As arrows in the hand of a mighty man; 
\q2 so are the children of those who were outcasts. 
\q1
\v 5 Blessed is the man who fills his desire with them: 
\q2 they will not be ashamed when they speak to their enemies in the gate. 
\c 127 
\d
\v 1 A Song of Ascents. 
\q1
\v 1b Blessed are all those who fear the Lord;
\q2 who walk in his ways. 
\q1
\v 2 You will eat the fruits of your labours: 
\q2 you are blessed, and it will be well with you. 
\q1
\v 3 Your wife will be as a fruitful vine on the sides of your house: 
\q2 your children as young olive-plants all around your table. 
\q1
\v 4 Behold, thus will a man be blessed who fears the Lord. 
\q1
\v 5 May the Lord bless you out of Zion; 
\q2 and may you see the good things of Jerusalem all the days of your life. 
\q1
\v 6 May you see your children's children. 
\q2 Peace be upon Israel. 
\c 128 
\d
\v 1 A Song of Ascents. 
\q1
\v 1b Often they warred against me from my youth, 
\q2 let Israel now say: 
\q1
\v 2 Often they warred against me from my youth: 
\q2 and yet they didn't prevail against me. 
\q1
\v 3 The sinners carved upon my back: 
\q2 they prolonged their lawlessness. 
\q1
\v 4 The righteous Lord has cut off the necks of sinners. 
\q1
\v 5 Let all who hate Zion be put to shame and turned back. 
\q1
\v 6 Let them be as the grass of the house-tops, 
\q2 which withers before it is plucked up. 
\q1
\v 7 With it the reaper doesn't fill his hand,
\q2 nor does he who gathers the sheaves fill his bosom. 
\q1
\v 8 Nor do those who pass by say, The blessing of the Lord be upon you: 
\q2 we have blessed you in the name of the Lord. 
\c 129 
\d
\v 1 A Song of Ascents. 
\q1
\v 1b Out of the depths have I cried to you, O Lord. 
\q1
\v 2 O Lord, listen to my voice;
\q2 let your ears be attentive to the voice of my supplication. 
\q1
\v 3 If you, O Lord, should mark iniquities, 
\q2 O Lord, who will stand? 
\q1
\v 4 For with you is \f + \fr 129:4 \fqa Or, \ft propitiation.\f*forgiveness.
\q1
\v 5 For the sake of your law I have waited for you, 
\q2 O Lord, my soul has waited for your word. 
\q1
\v 6 My soul has hoped in the Lord; 
\q2 from the morning watch until night;
\q2 from the morning watch let Israel hope in the Lord.
\q1
\v 7 For with the Lord is mercy,  
\q2 and with him is abundant redemption. 
\q1
\v 8 He will redeem Israel from all his iniquities. 
\c 130 
\d
\v 1 A Song of Ascents. Of David.
\q1
\v 1b O Lord, my heart isn't exalted, 
\q2 neither have my eyes been raised: 
\q2 neither have I exercised myself in great things, 
\q2 nor in things too wonderful for me. 
\q1
\v 2 \f + \fr 130:2 \ft The Greek of this verse is difficult. It begins with εἰ μὴ, which can be read either oath-like (“surely I was humble”) or conditionally (“if I was not humble …”), and ends with ὡς ἀνταπόδοσις (“like recompense”), which may be linked to the child-image or may express an implied curse or consequence.\f*Surely I was humble-minded, 
\q2 and lifted up my soul like a weaned child with its mother;
\q2 let recompense come upon my soul. 
\q1
\v 3 Let Israel hope in the Lord, from now on and forever. 
\c 131 
\d
\v 1 A Song of Ascents. 
\q1
\v 1b Lord, remember David, and all his humility: 
\q1
\v 2 how he swore to the Lord,
\q2 vowed to the God of Jacob,  
\q1
\v 3 \f + \fr 131:3 \fqa Gr. \ft if I shall, etc. \fqa Hebraism.\f*I will not go into the dwelling of my house; 
\q2 I will not go up to the couch of my bed; 
\q1
\v 4 I will not give sleep to my eyes, 
\q2 nor slumber to my eyelids, 
\q2 nor rest to my temples, 
\q1
\v 5 until I find a place for the Lord, 
\q2 a dwelling for the God of Jacob. 
\q1
\v 6 Behold, we heard of it in Ephratha; 
\q2 we found it in the fields of the forest. 
\q1
\v 7 We will enter into his dwellings: 
\q2 let us worship at the place where his feet stood. 
\q1
\v 8 Arise, O Lord, into your rest; 
\q2 you, and the ark of your holiness. 
\q1
\v 9 Your priests will clothe themselves with righteousness; 
\q2 and your holy ones will exult. 
\q1
\v 10 For the sake of your servant David don't turn away the face of your anointed. 
\q1
\v 11 The Lord swore truly to David, and he will not annul it, 
\q2 Of the fruit of your body will I set one upon your throne. 
\q1
\v 12 If your children will keep my covenant, 
\q2 and these my testimonies which I will teach them, 
\q2 their children also will sit upon your throne forever. 
\q1
\v 13 For the Lord chose Zion, 
\q2 he selected her for a habitation for himself, 
\q1
\v 14 This is my rest forever: 
\q2 here I will dwell; for I have chosen it. 
\q1
\v 15 I will surely bless her \f + \fr 131:15 \fqa Gr. \ft hunting, catch.\f*provision: 
\q2 I will satisfy her poor with bread. 
\q1
\v 16 I will clothe her priests with salvation; 
\q2 and her holy ones will greatly exult. 
\q1
\v 17 There will I cause to spring up a horn to David: 
\q2 I have prepared a lamp for my anointed. 
\q1
\v 18 His enemies I will clothe with shame; 
\q2 but upon him my \f + \fr 131:18 \fqa Gr. \ft holy thing, sanctuary, or consecration.\f*holiness will flourish. 
\c 132 
\d
\v 1 A Song of Ascents. Of David.
\q1
\v 1b Behold! What is so good, or what is so pleasant,
\q2 as for brothers to dwell together? 
\q1
\v 2 Like ointment on the head, that ran down to the beard, the beard of Aaron; 
\q2 that ran down to the hem of his clothing. 
\q1
\v 3 As the dew of Hermon, that comes down on the mountains of Zion: 
\q2 for there the Lord commanded the blessing: life forever. 
\c 133 
\d
\v 1 A Song of Ascents. 
\q1
\v 1b Behold! Bless the Lord, all the servants of the Lord, 
\q2 who stand in the house of the Lord, 
\q2 in the courts of the house of our God. 
\q1
\v 2 Lift up your hands by night toward the holy places,
\q2 and bless the Lord. 
\q1
\v 3 May the Lord, who made heaven and earth, bless you from Zion. 
\c 134 
\d
\v 1 Alleluia. 
\q1
\v 1b Praise the name of the Lord; 
\q2 praise the Lord, you servants, 
\q1
\v 2 who stand in the house of the Lord, 
\q2 in the courts of the house of our God. 
\q1
\v 3 Praise the Lord; for the Lord is good: 
\q2 sing praises to his name; for it is good. 
\q1
\v 4 For the Lord has chosen Jacob for himself, 
\q2 Israel for his treasured possession. 
\q1
\v 5 For I know that the Lord is great, 
\q2 and our Lord is above all gods; 
\q1
\v 6 all that the Lord willed, he did in heaven, and on the earth, 
\q2 in the sea, and in all deeps. 
\q1
\v 7 Who brings up clouds from the extremity of the earth: 
\q2 he has made lightnings for the rain: 
\q2 he brings winds out of his treasures. 
\q1
\v 8 Who struck the first-born of Egypt, 
\q2 both of man and beast. 
\q1
\v 9 He sent signs and wonders into the midst of you, O Egypt, 
\q2 on Pharaoh, and on all his servants. 
\q1
\v 10 Who struck many nations, 
\q2 and killed mighty kings; 
\q1
\v 11 Sihon king of the Amorites, and Og king of Bashan, 
\q2 and all the kingdoms of Canaan: 
\q1
\v 12 and gave their land as an inheritance, 
\q2 an inheritance to Israel his people. 
\q1
\v 13 O Lord, your name is forever; 
\q2 O Lord, your memorial is to all generations. 
\q1
\v 14 For the Lord will judge his people, 
\q2 and relent concerning his servants. 
\q1
\v 15 The idols of the nations are silver and gold, 
\q2 the works of men's hands. 
\q1
\v 16 They have a mouth, but do not speak; 
\q2 they have eyes, but do not see; 
\q1
\v 17 they have ears, but do not hear; 
\q2 \f + \fr 134:17 \ft Some Greek copies add: “they have noses, but do not smell; they have hands, but do not touch; they have feet, but do not walk; neither do they speak through their throat.” Rahlfs places these words in brackets.\f*for there is no breath in their mouth. 
\q1
\v 18 Let those who make them be made like them; 
\q2 and all those who trust in them. 
\q1
\v 19 O house of Israel, bless the Lord: 
\q2 O house of Aaron, bless the Lord: 
\q1
\v 20 O house of Levi, bless the Lord: 
\q2 you who fear the Lord, bless the Lord. 
\q1
\v 21 Blessed in Zion be the Lord, 
\q2 who dwells in Jerusalem. 
\c 135 
\d
\v 1 Alleluia. 
\q1
\v 1b Give thanks to the Lord: for he is good: 
\q2 for his mercy is forever. 
\q1
\v 2 Give thanks to the God of gods:
\q2 for his mercy is forever. 
\q1
\v 3 Give thanks to the Lord of lords: 
\q2 for his mercy is forever. 
\q1
\v 4 To him who alone has worked great wonders: 
\q2 for his mercy is forever. 
\q1
\v 5 To him who made the heavens by understanding; 
\q2 for his mercy is forever. 
\q1
\v 6 To him who established the earth on the waters; 
\q2 for his mercy is forever.  
\q1
\v 7 To him who alone made great lights; 
\q2 for his mercy is forever;  
\q1
\v 8 The sun to rule the day; 
\q2 for his mercy is forever; 
\q1
\v 9 The moon and the stars to rule the night; 
\q2 for his mercy is forever. 
\q1
\v 10 To him who struck Egypt with their first-born; 
\q2 for his mercy is forever;  
\q1
\v 11 Brought Israel out of their midst; 
\q2 for his mercy is forever; 
\q1
\v 12 with a strong hand, and a high arm: 
\q2 for his mercy is forever. 
\q1
\v 13 To him who divided the Red Sea into parts: 
\q2 for his mercy is forever; 
\q1
\v 14 and brought Israel through the midst of it: 
\q2 for his mercy is forever;  
\q1
\v 15 and overthrew Pharaoh and his host in the Red Sea: 
\q2 for his mercy is forever. 
\q1
\v 16 To him who led his people through the wilderness: 
\q2 for his mercy is forever. 
\q1
\v 17 To him who struck great kings: 
\q2 for his mercy is forever; 
\q1
\v 18 and killed mighty kings; 
\q2 for his mercy is forever; 
\q1
\v 19 Sihon king of the Amorites: 
\q2 for his mercy is forever; 
\q1
\v 20 and Og king of Bashan: 
\q2 for his mercy is forever;  
\q1
\v 21 and gave their land as an inheritance: 
\q2 for his mercy is forever;  
\q1
\v 22 an inheritance to Israel his servant: 
\q2 for his mercy is forever.  
\q1
\v 23 For in our humiliation the Lord remembered us; 
\q2 for his mercy is forever;  
\q1
\v 24 and redeemed us from our enemies; 
\q2 for his mercy is forever.  
\q1
\v 25 Who gives food to all flesh; 
\q2 for his mercy is forever.  
\q1
\v 26 Give thanks to the God of heaven; 
\q2 for his mercy is forever.  
\c 136 
\d
\v 1 Of David\f + \fr 136:1 \ft Some Greek copies add: “Of Jeremiah.”\f* 
\q1
\v 1b By the rivers of Babylon, there we sat; 
\q2 and wept when we remembered Zion. 
\q1
\v 2 We hung our \f + \fr 136:2 \fqa Gr. \ft instruments.\f*harps on the willows in its midst. 
\q1
\v 3 For there those who had taken us captive asked of us words of a song; 
\q2 and those who had carried us away \add asked for\add* a hymn, 
\q2 Sing us one of the songs of Zion. 
\q1
\v 4 How should we sing the Lord's song in a foreign land? 
\q1
\v 5 If I forget you, O Jerusalem, 
\q2 let my right hand be forgotten. 
\q1
\v 6 May my tongue cling to my throat, if I do not remember you; 
\q2 if I do not choose Jerusalem as the chief of my joy. 
\q1
\v 7 Remember, O Lord, the children of Edom in the day of Jerusalem; 
\q2 who said, Raze \add it\add*, \f + \fr 136:7 \fqa Gr. \ft empty, empty.\f*raze \add it\add*, even to its foundation. 
\q1
\v 8 Wretched daughter of Babylon! Blessed will he be who rewards you as you have rewarded us. 
\q1
\v 9 Blessed will he be who seizes and dashes your infants against the rock. 
\c 137 
\d
\v 1 Of David\f + \fr 137:1 \ft Some Greek copies add: “Of Haggai and Zechariah.”\f*
\q1
\v 1b I will give you thanks, O Lord, with my whole heart; 
\q2 and I will sing psalms to you before the angels; 
\q2 for you have heard the words of my mouth. 
\q1
\v 2 I will worship toward your holy temple, 
\q2 and give thanks to your name, 
\q2 on account of your mercy and your truth; 
\q2 for you have magnified your oracle above every name. 
\q1
\v 3 In whatever day I will call upon you, hear me speedily; 
\q2 you will greatly strengthen my soul with power.
\q1
\v 4 Let all the kings of the earth, O Lord, give thanks to you; 
\q2 for they have heard all the words of your mouth. 
\q1
\v 5 Let them sing in the ways of the Lord; 
\q2 for great is the glory of the Lord. 
\q1
\v 6 For the Lord is high, and regards the lowly; 
\q2 and he knows the lofty from afar. 
\q1
\v 7 If I walk in the midst of affliction, you will revive me; 
\q2 you will stretch forth your hand against the wrath of my enemies, 
\q2 and your right hand will save me. 
\q1
\v 8 The Lord will repay on my behalf: 
\q2 your mercy, O Lord, is forever: 
\q2 don't forsake the works of your hands. 
\c 138 
\d
\v 1 For the end. A Psalm of David.\f + \fr 138:1 \fqa Alex. \ft + of Zachariah in the dispersion.\f* 
\q1
\v 1b O Lord, you have proved me, and known me. 
\q1
\v 2 You know my sitting down and my rising up: 
\q2 you understand my thoughts from afar. 
\q1
\v 3 You have traced my path and my measuring line, 
\q2 and have foreseen all my ways. 
\q1
\v 4 For there is no word on my tongue; 
\q2 behold, O Lord, you have known all things, 
\q1
\v 5 the last and the first: 
\q2 you have fashioned me, and laid your hand upon me. 
\q1
\v 6 Your knowledge is too wonderful for me; 
\q2 it is too strong for me, I cannot \add attain\add* to it. 
\q1
\v 7 Where will I go from your Spirit? 
\q2 and where will I flee from your presence? 
\q1
\v 8 If I should go up to heaven, you are there: 
\q2 if I should go down to Hades, you are present. 
\q1
\v 9 If I take up my wings at dawn, 
\q2 and dwell at the ends of the sea,
\q1
\v 10 for even there your hand would guide me, 
\q2 and your right hand would hold me. 
\q1
\v 11 I said, Surely the darkness will cover me; 
\q2 yet night is light in my delight. 
\q1
\v 12 For darkness will not be darkness with you; 
\q2 but night will be light as day: 
\q2 as its darkness, so also its light. 
\q1
\v 13 For you, O Lord, have possessed my kidneys; 
\q2 you have helped me from my mother's womb. 
\q1
\v 14 I will give you thanks; 
\q2 for you are fearfully wondrous; 
\q2 wondrous are your works; and my soul knows \add it\add* well. 
\q1
\v 15 My bone which you made in secret was not hidden from you, 
\q2 nor my substance, in the lowest parts of the earth. 
\q1
\v 16 Your eyes saw my unwrought \add substance\add*, and all \add men\add* will be written in your book; 
\q2 they will be formed by day, though \add there should for a time\add* be no one among them. 
\q1
\v 17 But your friends, O God, have been greatly honoured; 
\q2 their rule has been greatly strengthened. 
\q1
\v 18 I will number them, and they will be multiplied beyond the sand; 
\q2 I awake, and am still with you. 
\q1
\v 19 Oh that you would kill the wicked, O God; 
\q2 depart from me, you men of blood. 
\q1
\v 20 \f + \fr 138:20 \ft The Greek of this verse is difficult.\f*For you will say concerning \add their\add* thought, 
\q2 \add that\add* they will take your cities in vain. 
\q1
\v 21 Have I not hated them, O Lord, that hate you? 
\q2 and wasted away because of your enemies? 
\q1
\v 22 I have hated them with perfect hatred; 
\q2 they became enemies to me.
\q1
\v 23 Prove me, O God, and know my heart; 
\q2 examine me, and know my paths; 
\q1
\v 24 and see if there is any way of lawlessness in me, 
\q2 and lead me in an everlasting way. 
\c 139 
\d
\v 1 For the end. A Psalm of David. 
\p
\q1
\v 2 Rescue me, O Lord, from the evil man; 
\q2 deliver me from the unjust man. 
\q1
\v 3 Who have devised injustice in their hearts; 
\q2 all day they stirred up wars. 
\q1
\v 4 They have sharpened their tongue like a snake; 
\q2 \x + \xo 139:4 \xt Rom. 3. 13.\x*the poison of asps is under their lips. \qs Pause.\qs* 
\q1
\v 5 Keep me, O Lord, from the hand of the sinner; 
\q2 rescue me from unjust men who have purposed to overthrow my goings. 
\q1
\v 6 The proud have hid a snare for me, and have stretched out ropes \add as\add* snares for my feet; 
\q2 they set a stumbling-block for me beside the path. \qs Pause.\qs* 
\q1
\v 7 I said to the Lord, You are my God; 
\q2 listen, O Lord, to the voice of my supplication. 
\q1
\v 8 O Lord, Lord, strength of my salvation; 
\q2 you have sheltered my head in the day of battle. 
\q1
\v 9 Don't deliver me, O Lord, to the sinner from my desire:
\q2 they have schemed against me; 
\q2 don't forsake me, lest they should be exalted. \qs Pause.\qs* 
\q1
\v 10 The head of those who surround me— 
\q2 the trouble of their lips will cover them. 
\q1
\v 11 Coals will fall upon them; 
\q2 and you will cast them down in fire: 
\q2 in afflictions they will not endure.
\q1
\v 12 A loose-tongued man will not prosper on the earth: 
\q2 evils will hunt the unrighteous man to destruction. 
\q1
\v 13 I know that the Lord will maintain the cause of the \f + \fr 139:13 \fqa Gr. \ft singular.\f*poor, 
\q2 and the right of the needy ones. 
\q1
\v 14 Surely the righteous will give thanks to your name: 
\q2 the upright will dwell in your presence. 
\c 140 
\d
\v 1 A Psalm of David. 
\q1
\v 1b O Lord, I have cried to you; hear me: 
\q2 pay attention to the voice of my supplication, when I cry to you. 
\q1
\v 2 Let my prayer be set forth before you as incense; 
\q2 the lifting up of my hands, an evening sacrifice. 
\q1
\v 3 Set a watch, O Lord, on my mouth, 
\q2 and a guarded door about my lips. 
\q1
\v 4 Don't incline my heart to words of wickedness, 
\q2 to \f + \fr 140:4 \fqa Gr. \ft pretend pretences.\f*employ pretexts in sins, with men who work lawlessness: 
\q2 and I will not unite with their chosen ones. 
\q1
\v 5 The righteous will chasten me with mercy, and reprove me: 
\q2 but don't let the oil of the sinner anoint my head: 
\q2 for yet my prayer will also be in their \f + \fr 140:5 \ft The Greek is difficult; “in their delights” may mean concerning the things they desire or prosper in.\f*delights. 
\q1
\v 6 Their judges have been swallowed up beside the rock: 
\q2 they will hear my words, for they are sweet. 
\q1
\v 7 As a lump of earth is crushed upon the ground, 
\q2 our bones have been scattered beside the grave. 
\q1
\v 8 For my eyes are to you, O Lord, Lord: 
\q2 I have hoped in you; don't take away my life. 
\q1
\v 9 Keep me from the snare which they have set for me, 
\q2 and from the stumbling-blocks of those who work lawlessness. 
\q1
\v 10 Sinners will fall in \f + \fr 140:10 \fqa Gr. \ft his net.\f*their own net: 
\q2 I am alone until I pass by. 
\c 141 
\d
\v 1 Of instruction. Of David, when he was in the cave. A Prayer. 
\q1
\v 2 I cried to the Lord with my voice;
\q2 with my voice I made supplication to the Lord. 
\q1
\v 3 I will pour out before him my supplication: 
\q2 I will declare before him my affliction. 
\q1
\v 4 When my spirit was fainting within me, 
\q2 you knew my paths; 
\q1 in the path where I walked, 
\q2 they hid a snare for me. 
\q1
\v 5 I looked to the right hand and saw, 
\q2 for there was no one who acknowledged me; 
\q1 refuge failed me; 
\q2 and there was no one who cared for my soul. 
\q1
\v 6 I cried to you, O Lord, 
\q2 and said, You are my hope, 
\q2 my portion in the land of the living. 
\q1
\v 7 Pay attention to my supplication, 
\q2 for I am brought very low; 
\q1 deliver me from those who persecute me; 
\q2 for they are stronger than I. 
\q1
\v 8 Bring my soul out of prison, 
\q2 that I may give thanks to your name, O Lord; 
\q1 the righteous will wait for me, 
\q2 until you reward me. 
\c 142 
\d
\v 1 A Psalm of David, when his son pursued him. 
\q1
\v 1b O Lord, pay attention to my prayer: 
\q2 listen to my supplication in your truth; 
\q2 hear me in your righteousness. 
\q1
\v 2 Don't enter into judgment with your servant, 
\q2 for in your sight no one living will be justified. 
\q1
\v 3 For the enemy has persecuted my soul; 
\q2 he has brought my life down to the ground; 
\q1 he has made me to dwell in a dark \add place\add*, 
\q2 like those who have been long dead. 
\q1
\v 4 Therefore my spirit grew faint upon me; 
\q2 my heart was troubled within me. 
\q1
\v 5 I remembered the days of old; 
\q2 and I meditated on all your doings: 
\q2 I meditated on the works of your hands. 
\q1
\v 6 I spread forth my hands to you; 
\q2 my soul \add thirsts\add* for you, like a dry land. \qs Pause.\qs* 
\q1
\v 7 Hear me speedily, O Lord; my spirit has failed; 
\q2 don't turn away your face from me, 
\q2 or I will be like those who go down to the pit. 
\q1
\v 8 Cause me to hear your mercy in the morning; 
\q2 for I have hoped in you; 
\q1 make known to me the way in which I will walk; 
\q2 for I have lifted up my soul to you. 
\q1
\v 9 Deliver me from my enemies, O Lord; 
\q2 for I have fled to you for refuge. 
\q1
\v 10 Teach me to do your will; for you are my God; 
\q2 your good Spirit will guide me in the land of uprightness. 
\q1
\v 11 You will revive me, O Lord, for your name's sake; 
\q2 in your righteousness you will bring my soul out of affliction. 
\q1
\v 12 In your mercy you will destroy my enemies, 
\q2 and will destroy all those that afflict my soul; 
\q2 for I am your servant. 
\c 143 
\d
\v 1 Of David. Concerning Goliath. 
\q1
\v 1b Blessed \add be\add* the Lord my God, 
\q2 who instructs my hands for battle,
\q2 my fingers for war. 
\q1
\v 2 My mercy, and my refuge; 
\q2 my helper, and my deliverer; 
\q2 my protector, in whom I have trusted; 
\q2 who subdues my people under me. 
\q1
\v 3 Lord, what is man, that you are made known to him? 
\q2 Or the son of man, that you take account of him? 
\q1
\v 4 Man is like vanity: 
\q2 his days pass by like a shadow. 
\q1
\v 5 O Lord, bow your heavens, and come down: 
\q2 touch the mountains, and they will smoke. 
\q1
\v 6 Send lightning, and you will scatter them: 
\q2 send forth your arrows, and you will confound them. 
\q1
\v 7 Send forth your hand from on high; 
\q2 rescue me, and deliver me out of many waters, 
\q2 out of the hand of the sons of foreigners; 
\q1
\v 8 whose mouth has spoken vanity, 
\q2 and their right hand is a right hand of wickedness. 
\q1
\v 9 O God, I will sing a new song to you: 
\q2 I will play to you on a psaltery of ten strings. 
\q1
\v 10 To him who gives \f + \fr 143:10 \fqa Or, \ft victory.\f*salvation to kings: 
\q2 who redeems his servant David from the evil sword. 
\q1
\v 11 Deliver me, and rescue me from the hand of the sons of foreigners, 
\q2 whose mouth has spoken vanity, and their right hand is a right hand of wickedness; 
\q1
\v 12 whose children are as plants, firmly planted in their youth: 
\q2 their daughters are beautiful, sumptuously adorned after the likeness of a temple. 
\q1
\v 13 Their garners are full, and bursting with one kind of store after another; 
\q2 their sheep are prolific, multiplying in their fields. 
\q1
\v 14 Their oxen are fat: 
\q2 there is no breach of wall, nor going out, 
\q2 nor cry in their streets. 
\q1
\v 15 Men bless the people to whom these things belong; 
\q2 blessed is the people whose God is the Lord. 
\c 144 
\d
\v 1 A praise. Of David.
\q1
\v 1b I will exalt you, my God, my king; 
\q2 and I will bless your name forever, and forever and ever. 
\q1
\v 2 Every day will I bless you, 
\q2 and I will praise your name forever, and forever and ever. 
\q1
\v 3 The Lord is great, and greatly to be praised; 
\q2 and there is no end of his greatness. 
\q1
\v 4 Generation after generation will praise your works, 
\q2 and tell of your power. 
\q1
\v 5 They will speak of the glorious majesty of your holiness, 
\q2 and recount your wonders. 
\q1
\v 6 They will speak of the power of your fearsome \add acts\add*; 
\q2 and recount your greatness. 
\q1
\v 7 They will pour forth the memory of the abundance of your goodness, 
\q2 and will exult in your righteousness. 
\q1
\v 8 The Lord is compassionate, and merciful; 
\q2 long-suffering, and abundant in mercy. 
\q1
\v 9 The Lord is good to all, 
\q2 and his compassions are over all his works. 
\q1
\v 10 Let all your works, O Lord, give thanks to you; 
\q2 and let your saints bless you. 
\q1
\v 11 They will speak of the glory of your kingdom, 
\q2 and talk of your dominion; 
\q1
\v 12 to make known to the sons of men your power, 
\q2 and the glorious majesty of your kingdom. 
\q1
\v 13 Your kingdom is \f + \fr 144:13 \fqa Gr. \ft a kingdom of all ages.\f*an everlasting kingdom, 
\q2 and your dominion \add endures\add* \f + \fr 144:13 \fqa Gr. \ft in every generation and generation.\f*through all generations. 
\q1
\v 13a The Lord is faithful in his words, 
\q2 and holy in all his works. 
\p
\q1
\v 14 The Lord supports all who are falling, 
\q2 and sets up all who are broken down. 
\q1
\v 15 The eyes of all hope in you; 
\q2 and you give \add them\add* their food in due season. 
\q1
\v 16 You open your hands, 
\q2 and fill every living thing with favour. 
\q1
\v 17 The Lord is righteous in all his ways, 
\q2 and holy in all his works. 
\q1
\v 18 The Lord is near to all who call upon him, 
\q2 to all who call upon him in truth. 
\q1
\v 19 He will perform the desire of those who fear him: 
\q2 and he will hear their supplication, and save them. 
\q1
\v 20 The Lord preserves all who love him: 
\q2 but all sinners he will completely destroy. 
\q1
\v 21 My mouth will speak the praise of the Lord: 
\q2 and let all flesh bless his holy name forever, and forever and ever. 
\c 145 
\d
\v 1 Alleluia. Of Haggai and Zechariah. 
\q1
\v 1b My soul, praise the Lord. 
\q1
\v 2 While I live will I praise the Lord: 
\q2 I will sing praises to my God as long as I exist. 
\q1
\v 3 Don't trust in princes, 
\q2 nor in the children of men, 
\q2 in whom there is no salvation. 
\q1
\v 4 His breath will go forth, 
\q2 and he will return to the earth; 
\q2 in that day all his thoughts will perish. 
\q1
\v 5 Blessed is he whose helper is the God of Jacob, 
\q2 whose hope is in the Lord his God: 
\q1
\v 6 who made heaven, and earth, the sea, and all things in them: 
\q2 who keeps truth forever: 
\q1
\v 7 who executes justice for the wronged: 
\q2 who gives food to the hungry. 
\q2 The Lord looses the fettered ones: 
\q1
\v 8 the Lord makes wise the blind: 
\p The Lord raises up the broken down: 
\q2 the Lord loves the righteous: 
\q2 the Lord preserves the strangers; 
\q1
\v 9 he will uphold the orphan and widow: 
\q2 but will completely remove the way of sinners. 
\q1
\v 10 The Lord will reign forever, 
\q2 your God, O Zion, to all generations. 
\c 146 
\d
\v 1 Alleluia. Of Haggai and Zechariah. 
\q1
\v 1b Praise the Lord: for singing psalms is good; 
\q2 let praise be sweet to our God. 
\q1
\v 2 The Lord builds up Jerusalem; 
\q2 and he will gather together the dispersed of Israel. 
\q1
\v 3 He heals the broken in heart, 
\q2 and binds up their wounds. 
\q1
\v 4 He numbers the multitudes of stars; 
\q2 and calls them all by name. 
\q1
\v 5 Great is our Lord, and great is his strength; 
\q2 and his understanding is infinite. 
\q1
\v 6 The Lord lifts up the meek; 
\q2 but brings sinners down to the ground. 
\q1
\v 7 Begin \add the song\add* with thanksgiving to the Lord; 
\q2 sing praises on the harp to our God: 
\q1
\v 8 who covers the heavens with clouds, 
\q2 who prepares rain for the earth, 
\q2 who causes grass to spring up on the mountains, 
\q2 [\f + \fr 146:8 \ft See Ps \xt 103. 14.\f*and green herb for the service of men;] 
\q1
\v 9 and gives to cattle their food, 
\q2 and to the young ravens that call upon him. 
\q1
\v 10 He will not take pleasure in the strength of a horse; 
\q2 neither is he well-pleased with the legs of a man. 
\q1
\v 11 The Lord takes pleasure in those who fear him, 
\q2 and in those who hope in his mercy.
\b
\c 147 
\d
\v 1 Alleluia. Of Haggai and Zechariah.\f + \fr 147:1 \ft In the original text, the following verses are numbered 12 to 20.\f* 
\q1
\v 1b Praise the Lord, O Jerusalem; 
\q2 praise your God, O Zion. 
\q1
\v 2 For he has strengthened the bars of your gates; 
\q2 he has blessed your children within you. 
\q1
\v 3 He makes your borders peaceful, 
\q2 and fills you with the \f + \fr 147:3 \fqa Lit. \ft fat of wheat.\f*flour of wheat. 
\q1
\v 4 He sends his oracle to the earth: 
\q2 his word will run swiftly. 
\q1
\v 5 He gives snow like wool: 
\q2 he scatters the mist like ashes. 
\q1
\v 6 Casting \add forth\add* his ice like morsels: 
\q2 who will stand before his cold? 
\q1
\v 7 He will send out his word, and melt them: 
\q2 he will blow \add with\add* his wind, and the waters will flow. 
\q1
\v 8 He sends his word to Jacob, 
\q2 his ordinances and judgments to Israel. 
\q1
\v 9 He has not done so to \f + \fr 147:9 \fqa Gr. \ft every.\f*any \add other\add* nation; 
\q2 and he has not shown them his judgments. 
\c 148 
\d
\v 1 Alleluia. Of Haggai and Zechariah. 
\q1
\v 1b Praise the Lord from the heavens:
\q2 praise him in the highest. 
\q1
\v 2 Praise him, all his angels: 
\q2 praise him, all his hosts. 
\q1
\v 3 Praise him, sun and moon: 
\q2 praise him, all you stars and light. 
\q1
\v 4 Praise him, you heavens of heavens, 
\q2 and the water that is above the heavens. 
\q1
\v 5 Let them praise the name of the Lord: 
\q2 for he spoke, and they were made; 
\q2 he commanded, and they were created. 
\q1
\v 6 He has established them forever, even forever and ever: 
\q2 he has made an ordinance, and it will not pass away. 
\q1
\v 7 Praise the Lord from the earth, you \f + \fr 148:7 \fqa Gr. \ft δράκοντες, traditionally 'dragons'; here, mighty sea creatures.\f*mighty serpents, and all deeps. 
\q1
\v 8 Fire, hail, snow, ice, stormy wind; 
\q2 the things that perform his word. 
\q1
\v 9 Mountains, and all hills; 
\q2 fruitful trees, and all cedars: 
\q1
\v 10 wild beasts, and all cattle; 
\q2 reptiles, and winged birds: 
\q1
\v 11 kings of the earth, and all peoples; 
\q2 princes, and all judges of the earth: 
\q1
\v 12 young men and virgins, 
\q2 old men with youths: 
\q1
\v 13 let them praise the name of the Lord: 
\q2 for his name only is exalted; 
\q2 his praise is upon earth and heaven, 
\q1
\v 14 and he will exalt the horn of his people, 
\q2 \add there is\add* a hymn for all his saints, 
\q2 of the children of Israel, 
\q2 a people who draw near to him. 
\c 149 
\d
\v 1 Alleluia. 
\q1
\v 1b Sing to the Lord a new song: 
\q2 his praise is in the assembly of the saints. 
\q1
\v 2 Let Israel rejoice in the one who made him; 
\q2 and let the children of Zion exult in their king. 
\q1
\v 3 Let them praise his name in the dance: 
\q2 let them sing praises to him with timbrel and psaltery. 
\q1
\v 4 For the Lord takes pleasure in his people; 
\q2 and will exalt the meek with salvation. 
\q1
\v 5 The saints will rejoice in glory; 
\q2 and will exult on their beds. 
\q1
\v 6 The high praises of God will be in their throat, 
\q2 and two-edged swords in their hands; 
\q1
\v 7 to execute vengeance on the nations, 
\q2 rebukes among the peoples; 
\q1
\v 8 to bind their kings with fetters, 
\q2 and their nobles with manacles of iron; 
\q1
\v 9 to execute on them the written judgment: 
\q2 this honour have all his saints. 
\c 150 
\d
\v 1 Alleluia. 
\q1
\v 1b Praise God in his holy places: 
\q2 praise him in the firmament of his power. 
\q1
\v 2 Praise him on \add account of\add* his mighty acts: 
\q2 praise him according to his abundant greatness. 
\q1
\v 3 Praise him with the sound of a trumpet: 
\q2 praise him with psaltery and harp. 
\q1
\v 4 Praise him with timbrel and dance: 
\q2 praise him with strings and instruments. 
\q1
\v 5 Praise him with melodious cymbals: 
\q2 praise him with loud cymbals. 
\q1
\v 6 Let everything that has breath praise the Lord. 
\c 151 
\d
\v 1 This Psalm is David's own, and composed outside the number, when he fought in single combat with Goliath.
\q1 I was small among my brothers, and youngest in my father's house:
\q2 I tended my father's sheep. 
\q1
\v 2 My hands formed a musical instrument, 
\q2 and my fingers tuned a psaltery. 
\q1
\v 3 Who will report to my Lord? 
\q2 The Lord himself, he himself hears. 
\q1
\v 4 He sent his angel, and took me from my father's sheep, 
\q2 and he anointed me with the oil of his anointing. 
\q1
\v 5 My brothers were handsome and tall; 
\q2 but the Lord did not take pleasure in them. 
\q1
\v 6 I went out to meet the Philistine; 
\q2 and he cursed me by his idols. 
\q1
\v 7 But I drew his own sword, and beheaded him, 
\q2 and removed reproach from the children of Israel. 
